<article class="env-remark" id="0H4U">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H4U">Remark <span data-tag="0H4U">62.5.6</span> <span class="named">(Support)</span>.</a>  Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type. Let $r \geq 0$ be an integer. Let $\alpha $ be a family of $r$-cycles on fibres of $X/S$. We define the <em>support</em> of $\alpha $ to be </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Supp}(\alpha ) = \bigcup \nolimits _{s \in S} \text{Supp}(\alpha _ s) \subset X  \]
</div>
  <p> Here $\text{Supp}(\alpha _ s) \subset X_ s$ is the support of the cycle $\alpha _ s$, see Chow Homology, Definition <a href="/tag/0H46" data-tag="0H46">42.8.3</a>. The support $\text{Supp}(\alpha )$ is rarely a closed subset of $X$. </p>
</article>